  <p>My first automobile, purchased from Dan McCaulley for $20 in 1942. A very dependable truck that served me in work and play until 1951 when I sold it to a fellow from Del Norte for $20. The dragline boom visible in the background was connected to the first power shovel we had seen and brought the Dallas Filley family to Creede in the early '30s. Dallas ran the machine with boom attachment to set the heavy, steel pipe in place at the Santa Maria Reservoir. In 1943 William Kolisch Sr. fired up the old brute and loaded it on a flatcar at the depot for shipment to a coastal port, then on to Russia as part of the lend lease agreement we were told. The house in the background on the hill belonged to George Horne, the only black man in Creede and our good neighbor for years.</p>

